    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=537225997": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Director of Creative Marketing Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type FTS Required Degree 4 Year Degree Manage Others Yes Minimum Experience 5 Years Contact information Name Fawn McCracken Email mccrackenf@crown.edu Description The Director of Creative Marketing provides strategic and hands-on leadership for Crown College’s creative marketing, organic social media, multimedia storytelling, and visual brand execution. Reporting to the Vice President of Enrollment & Marketing, the Director develops and implements creative strategies that advance enrollment, strengthen institutional reputation, cultivate community engagement, and support donor and constituent relationships. The Director leads the College’s social media presence; directs the development of video, photography, design, and multimedia content; manages creative workflow; and ensures that public-facing content reflects Crown’s identity as a boldly Christian institution. The position supervises the Content Producer and assigned student workers and collaborates closely with internal stakeholders and external partners. Equipment Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, a personal computer and required software, cameras and multimedia-production equipment, printers, scanners, copy machines, and other equipment required by the position. Reports to Vice President of Enrollment & Marketing Essential Functions of the Job 25% CREATIVE MARKETING AND BRAND EXECUTION · Develop and execute an integrated creative marketing strategy aligned with Crown College’s mission, brand promise, strategic priorities, enrollment goals, and advancement objectives. · Translate institutional and enrollment priorities into compelling creative concepts, campaigns, and audience-centered content. · Provide creative direction for digital, social, print, video, photography, and multimedia projects. · Ensure consistent application of Crown’s brand standards, visual identity, tone, and Christian mission across channels and deliverables. · Partner with the Director of Communications to align institutional messaging with creative execution and channel strategy. · Advise the Vice President of Enrollment & Marketing on creative opportunities, emerging trends, audience engagement, and resource needs. 30% SOCIAL MEDIA · Develop and execute a comprehensive organic social media strategy promoting Crown’s brand, academic programs, student experience, events, outcomes, and strategic initiatives. · Create, curate, edit, schedule, and publish engaging text, image, video, and multimedia content across Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, X, YouTube, and emerging platforms. · Create, curate, and schedule content for the President’s social media channels in coordination with appropriate institutional leaders. · Develop and maintain a coordinated social media calendar that balances enrollment, institutional, advancement, athletics, academic, and community priorities. · Provide active community management by monitoring and responding to comments, messages, mentions, and inquiries in a timely, professional, and mission-consistent manner. · Monitor platform data, audience behavior, engagement, reach, traffic, and content performance using Sprout Social, native platform analytics, Google Analytics, and related tools; use findings to improve strategy and execution. · Collaborate with the Social Media Leadership Committee and campus departments to maintain consistency, quality, coordination, and institutional standards. · Establish procedures for account governance, access, moderation, archiving, escalation, and response to sensitive or emerging issues. · Stay current on platform changes, algorithms, accessibility expectations, best practices, and emerging content formats. · Train and equip student workers, interns, alumni, ambassadors, and campus contributors who participate in social media initiatives. 20% MULTIMEDIA STORYTELLING AND CONTENT PRODUCTION · Lead the planning and production of video, photography, short-form content, interviews, campaign assets, and institutional storytelling. · Supervise the Content Producer and provide clear briefs, priorities, timelines, feedback, and creative direction. · Identify stories and visual opportunities that communicate Crown’s mission, student experience, academic quality, community, and impact. · Ensure multimedia content is technically strong, accessible, appropriately licensed, and prepared for effective use across platforms. · Maintain an organized, searchable, and appropriately governed library of creative assets, releases, project files, and final deliverables. · Balance event coverage with strategic enrollment, institutional storytelling, and campaign-production priorities. 15% CREATIVE SERVICES, CAMPAIGNS, AND CROSS-FUNCTIONAL COLLABORATION · Manage creative intake, project briefs, prioritization, production calendars, review cycles, approvals, and delivery across multiple concurrent projects. · Collaborate with Enrollment and Communications leaders to develop audience-focused campaigns, organic channel support, and recruitment materials. · Execute print requests in collaboration with the content producer. · Provide approved creative assets and content support to external marketing partners and collaborate to ensure timely, emotive, brand-aligned campaign execution. · Partner with the Data team to review content and channel performance, support tracking requirements, and apply data-informed insights to creative testing and optimization. · Coordinate with the President’s Office,  Advancement, Athletics, Academics, Student Development, Operations and other areas to meet institutional priorities. · Manage relationships with approved photographers, videographers, freelancers, vendors, and production partners as assigned. · Ensure projects meet accessibility, copyright, licensing, privacy, release, and institutional policy requirements. 10% PERSONNEL LEADERSHIP, ADMINISTRATION, AND CONTINUOUS IMPROVEMENT · Recruit, onboard, coach, supervise, and evaluate the Content Producer and assigned student workers. · Establish team goals, work plans, production standards, service expectations, and professional-development priorities. · Monitor relevant budgets, subscriptions, equipment, vendors, and production expenses within delegated authority. · Develop and report appropriate creative and social media performance measures to the Vice President of Enrollment & Marketing. · Maintain documentation, templates, calendars, account access, workflows, and continuity plans for critical creative-marketing functions. · Participate in departmental and institutional meetings, planning, events, and professional development. · Perform other duties as assigned. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities · Strong desire to advance Christ-centered higher education through creative excellence and servant leadership. · Advanced understanding of social media platforms, audience behavior, algorithms, content formats, community management, and channel best practices. · Demonstrated ability to develop creative strategy and translate institutional goals into compelling, audience-centered content. · Excellent written, visual, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. · Proficiency with social media management and analytics tools such as Sprout Social, Meta Business Suite, YouTube Studio, Google Analytics, and comparable platforms. · Proficiency with content-creation and creative-production tools such as Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva, video-editing software, photography tools, and related technologies. · Strong understanding of photography, videography, editing, multimedia production, and digital asset management. · Ability to interpret analytics, identify actionable insights, and optimize content based on audience and performance data. · Strong creative judgment and the ability to protect and consistently apply institutional brand standards. · Ability to supervise, coach, motivate, and develop professional employees and student workers. · Excellent project-management, prioritization, organizational, and problem-solving skills in a fast-paced environment. · Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, manage sensitive issues, and collaborate effectively across departments. · Understanding of accessibility, copyright, licensing, permissions, privacy, and ethical content practices. · High level of personal integrity, professionalism, initiative, adaptability, and attention to detail. · Agreement with and commitment to the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. Physical Demands The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to perform the essential functions of this position successfully. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. · Sit or stand for extended periods and perform extensive computer and mobile-device work. · Possess hand and arm dexterity, or an equivalent ability, sufficient for keyboard use and operation of creative-production equipment. · Communicate effectively with coworkers, students, partners, and constituents by telephone, video conference, and in person. · Possess adequate vision to accommodate frequent viewing of computer screens and review of visual content. · Frequently lift or move up to 10 pounds and infrequently lift or move up to 25 pounds, including production equipment. · Occasionally move throughout campus and off-campus locations and work in moderate-to-high noise environments during events. Minimum Qualifications · Agreement with and commitment to abide by the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. · Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, digital media, visual communications, public relations, or a related field. · Five years of progressively responsible experience in creative marketing, social media, content strategy, digital communications, multimedia production, or a related area. · Demonstrated experience developing and executing social media strategy, creating content, managing online communities, and using analytics to guide decisions. · Demonstrated experience directing or producing video, photography, graphic, and multimedia content. · Experience managing complex projects, production calendars, and cross-functional stakeholders. · Supervisory experience or demonstrated experience leading employees, interns, students, vendors, or project teams. · A portfolio demonstrating strong creative judgment and effective content across multiple platforms. Preferred Qualifications · Master’s degree in marketing, communications, digital media, business, higher education, or a related field. · Seven or more years of progressively responsible experience in creative marketing or communications. · Experience in higher education, nonprofit, ministry, or faith-based organizations. · Experience leading creative services or content-production function. · Experience supporting enrollment marketing, advancement, executive social media, or institutional reputation initiatives. · Advanced experience with Adobe Creative Cloud, Sprout Social, Google Analytics, content-management systems, and digital asset-management tools. · Crown College alumnus or familiarity with Crown College and The Christian and Missionary Alliance. Benefits Crown College offers a generous and comprehensive benefits package for full-time staff and faculty, designed to support the health, well-being, and financial future of our employees. Benefits include medical coverage through Medica, dental coverage through Delta Dental, and vision coverage through EyeMed. Employees also receive employer-paid basic life insurance equal to one times their annual salary, subject to policy limits, with optional voluntary benefits including supplemental life insurance, hospital indemnity, critical illness, and short-term disability coverage. A Health Savings Account (HSA) is available for employees enrolled in the high-deductible health plan. In addition to competitive benefits, Crown offers generous paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay, along with a 403(b) retirement plan that includes an employer contribution. Environment and Location Employees enjoy working on our beautiful lakeside campus, which features an on-campus fitness center, scenic walking paths leading to Parley Lake and convenient access to our on-campus Frisbie Golf Course. These amenities provide excellent opportunities to stay active, recharge, and enjoy the natural beauty of the campus throughout the year. Non-Discrimination Policy Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status regarding public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.  This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.  Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate all job duties as determined necessary.) Additional Information Base Pay From 55,000 Base Pay To 65,000 Base Pay Per Year"
    },
    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=537208004": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type FTF Required Degree Masters Manage Others Yes Description This is a full time, tenure-track faculty position within the School of Health and Science teaching undergraduate nursing courses on campus and supervising nursing students in clinical settings. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of the Department of Nursing. SUPERVISION RECEIVED This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Nursing, the Dean of the School of Health and Science, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS Adjunct and clinical faculty who may be assigned within a course. EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION Works from an office at Crown College. Regular attendance on campus to complete job duties is required. Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and related software, printer, copy machines, Nursing Simulation Lab equipment and tools related to undergraduate teaching and research. Travel to clinical sites will also be required. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB · Teach courses within the prescribed nursing curriculum utilizing a variety of teaching methodologies to engage students in the learning process. A normal teaching load is 24 credits each year. · Teaching in simulation lab · Facilitate student development of knowledge, skills, and demeanor required for professional practice as a nurse. · Supervise students in clinical settings. · Advise students in the Department of Nursing. · Stay abreast of scholarly developments in specific and relevant fields as well as current teaching methodologies, curriculum development, and assessment. · Contribute to the field of nursing and/or the profession of college-level teaching. · Participate in measures to maintain compliance with Minnesota State Board of Nursing and Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education. · Support the mission, goals and objectives of Crown College. · Engage in general faculty responsibilities that include: o Participation in department and faculty meetings, o Care of students, o Crown College committee assignments, and o At least 10 hours of scheduled office hours on campus per week to be available to students. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES · Demonstrated experience and expertise teaching nursing courses at the college level. · Demonstrated experience in simulation labs. · Strong interpersonal skills and an enthusiasm for working with students pursuing higher education. · Established ability to work effectively as a team member. · Demonstrate excellence and professionalism in spoken, written and electronic communication skills when with prospective and current students, faculty, and staff, as well as clinical agency representatives. · Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith. · Experience evaluating students’ work and reporting results promptly. · Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. · Must be a committed Christian who is active in a local church PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time (in the classroom, in the simulation lab, and in clinical settings). Mobility to allow for safe movement within lab and clinical environments. Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for patient care, safe use of equipment, and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry. Vocal strength to speak clearly in a classroom and lab for extended periods of time. Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials. Body strength to frequently lift and/ or move up to ten (10) pounds. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS · Master of Science in Nursing or equivalent degree · Relevant experience as a nurse · Current unencumbered RN License · Demonstrated teaching effectiveness · Current American Heart Association Healthcare Provider BLS Certification (or equivalent). · Experience using computer technology in the teaching/learning process PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications) · Earned DNP, PhD in Nursing or other equivalent terminal degree. · Experience as a nurse in OB, acute medical/surgical, ICU, Emergency, or related area. · Unencumbered RN Licensure in Minnesota · 3+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education · Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments, especially related to the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education and the Minnesota Board of Nursing · Experience with advising BENEFITS Crown College offers a generous and comprehensive benefits package for full-time staff and faculty, designed to support the health, well-being, and financial future of our employees. Benefits include medical coverage through Medica, dental coverage through Delta Dental, and vision coverage through EyeMed. Employees also receive employer-paid basic life insurance equal to one times their annual salary, subject to policy limits, with optional voluntary benefits including supplemental life insurance, hospital indemnity, critical illness, and short-term disability coverage. A Health Savings Account (HSA) is available for employees enrolled in the high-deductible health plan. In addition to competitive benefits, Crown offers generous paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay, along with a 403(b) retirement plan that includes an employer contribution. ENVIRONMENT AND LOCATION Employees enjoy working on our beautiful lakeside campus, which features an on-campus fitness center, scenic walking paths leading to Parley Lake and convenient access to our on-campus Frisbie Golf Course. These amenities provide excellent opportunities to stay active, recharge, and enjoy the natural beauty of the campus throughout the year. Non-Discrimination Policy Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status regarding public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.  This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.  Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate all job duties as determined necessary.) Additional Information Base Pay From $62,000 Base Pay To $73,000"
    },
    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=537207621": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position- Registrar Office Assistant Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student Contact information Name Hannah Goodall Email registrar@crown.edu Description Anticipated Start Date: 26 Aug 2026 Hours Worked Per Week: 10 hours per week during M-T-W-R-F, 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM Job Definition - Registrar’s Office student workers support staff by performing routine duties and assisting with projects related to student data management and academic records. Supervisor Name Hannah Goodall Supervisor Title Assistant Registrar Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. Evidence of Christian character and a commitment to encourage others toward Christ-likeness. Maintain a 2.0 cumulative GPA. Must be in good standing with the college. Previous experience with administrative work preferred. Responsibilities - Maintain student electronic files and computer data with accuracy, efficiency, and confidentiality. Scan & link MDE forms FERPA Personal Information Updates Digitizing hard copy documents 30-day review Process student-related forms. Process internet submissions Student requests Name/address changes Transcript requests Transcript transfer entry Assist with the day-to-day operations of the office Courteous counter service Professional phone communication Email and print communications. Assist with editing Academic Catalog. Collaborate with Office of the Registrar staff in completing additional duties as needed. Data cleanup Research Graduation duties Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High attention to detail and accuracy in completing tasks. Proficiency with basic computer applications, including email and word processing. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Interpersonal skills. Strong customer service orientation with a friendly and helpful demeanor. Maintain confidentiality regarding private student information. Demonstrated dependability and punctuality. Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities. Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team. Strong problem-solving skills and ability to respond appropriately to unexpected situations. Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace. Physical Demands: Ability to lift and carry loads of up to 4 pounds. Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while performing job duties. Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay Per Hour"
    },
    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=520479623": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Assistant/ Associate Registrar Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type FTS Required Degree 4 Year Degree Manage Others Yes Minimum Experience 2 Years Description EFFECTIVE DATE: September 1, 2026 FLSA STATUS: Non-Exempt HOURS WORKED: 8:00 – 4:30, Monday-Friday, evenings, and weekends as needed The Assistant/Associate Registrar is part of the Registrar’s Office Team and is primarily responsible for transfer credit data management as well as advising and records-related processes and procedures. Additional responsibilities may include assisting with advising and advisor training. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: The Associate Registrar serves as a member of the Registrar’s Office team and reports to the Registrar. SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: Student workers EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from the Office of the Registrar at Crown College. Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, computer, printer, scanner, fax machine, copy machines, and other equipment as the position requires. At times, duties could involve some evening or weekend hours on the Crown College main campus. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: Maintain accurate student electronic files and computer data. Manage projects, policies, procedures, and correspondence in consultation with the registrar. Assist with the day-to-day operations of the office, including customer service in person, over the phone, and by email. Manage the student transfer process, including evaluation in collaboration with Deans and content experts, application of credits to degree records, and maintenance of the database (currently TES). Supervise student staff entering evaluation requests and manage data entry when student workers are not available. Collaborate with the Enrollment department to facilitate understanding of the transfer process and utilization of the tools. Maintain the degree audit software (currently Jenzabar). Process major/minor/catalog changes and verify the accuracy of the degree audit Process course substitutions and exceptions in the student record. Edit and update degree audits annually when curriculum updates are published in the Crown College Catalog. Assist with updating student academic plans annually. Meet with students to address questions related to transfer credit, degree audits, and academic plans. Coordinate the department and program application and approval processes with faculty advisors and chairs. Assist with Commencement planning and implementation. Review Graduate, Adult, and Professional graduation applications to determine student eligibility in collaboration with the academic advisor. Serve on related committees and task forces as assigned. Other duties as assigned. For qualified candidates with substantial experience in academic advising: Develop and implement appropriate training resources and tools for faculty academic advisors. Serve as the primary advising resource for faculty academic advisors. Work collaboratively with the Executive Director of Academic Achievement to facilitate effective advising for students. Serve as advisor for assigned students. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Detail-oriented and able to multitask. Ability to learn quickly and make decisions. Experience using Microsoft Office software (Word, Excel, Access). Experience using a Student Information System (such as Jenzabar). Experience using a document imaging system (such as Perceptive Content of Softdocs). Experience using transfer credit software (such as TES or Transferology). Superior customer service and keyboarding skills. Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those that an employee must meet to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sit for extended periods of time. To have hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for extensive use of a keyboard for data entry. To talk and hear with enough proficiency to allow for communicating with co-workers and applicants by phone or in person. To have adequate vision to accommodate frequent viewing of computer screens. The employee must frequently lift and/ or move up to ten (10) pounds and infrequently lift or move up to 25 pounds. The noise level is usually moderate. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: ·         Bachelor’s degree ·         2-3 years of experience working with student records, preferably in a Registrar’s department ·         Working knowledge of applicable laws, standards and regulations for higher education including but not limited to FERPA and AACRAO as well as familiarity with federal financial aid guidelines PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): ·         Master’s degree (or higher) ·         Education and/or experience in academic advising NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.  This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.  Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate any and all job duties as necessary. Additional Information Base Pay From 45,000 Base Pay To 50,000 Base Pay Per Year"
    },
    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=520433365": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Faculty In Residence - Worship Ministry Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type FIR Required Degree Masters Manage Others Yes Description This is a part-time faculty position to teach undergraduate worship ministry courses on campus within the School of Arts and Sciences. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of the Department of Biblical, Theological, and Ministry Studies. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Biblical, Theological, and Ministry Studies, the Dean of the School of Liberal Arts, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: Assigned students involved in chapel worship leadership and traveling worship teams EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College.  Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and required programs, printer, fax machine, calculator, copy machines, and other equipment as the position requires. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: · Teach two courses per normal academic term related to worship ministry. Courses may include  Technology in Worship, Performance and Practice in Worship Ministry, Worship Ministry Foundations and Practice, and/or supervision of student worship leaders. Additional topics and/or private music lessons may be available to qualified candidates. · Hold an average of at least 6 office hours per week during the normal academic terms. · Advise Worship Ministry students in the Department of Biblical, Theological, and Ministry Studies. · Recruit new students to pursue BA in Worship Ministry or minor in Worship Ministry. · Review related curricula and recommend modifications as appropriate · Participate in department and faculty meetings as available · Assist in securing adjunct instructors for worship classes and music instruction May also assist in mentoring and preparing worship leaders for on-campus Chapel worship and off-campus events by invitation REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: · A Biblically-grounded and convictional theology of worship · Demonstrated experience and expertise leading and teaching others to lead corporate worship · Ability to perform vocally or instrumentally from standard musical notation, chord charts, and lead sheets · Experience working with audio, video, and lighting equipment related to corporate worship · Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education · Established ability to work effectively as a team member · Skill to organize and manage multiple tasks simultaneously · Demonstrated excellence in spoken, written and electronic communication skills · Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith · Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time in classroom and corporate worship environments Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for safe use of equipment and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry Vocal strength to speak clearly in classroom and worship contexts for extended periods of time Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials Body strength to frequently lift and/or move up to twenty-five (25) pounds MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: · Bachelor’s degree in worship, music, or related field and a Master‘s degree with at least 18 hours in the field(s) of worship/ministry leadership/music or the equivalent professional experience · Significant experience leading corporate worship in an Evangelical church · Experience using technology in teaching/learning processes, team organization, and tools related to corporate worship PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): · MDiv, ThD, PhD, or the equivalent from an Evangelical seminary or graduate school · Ordination or Consecration in the Christian and Missionary Alliance · Collegiate teaching experience · Education and skills to teach private lessons in voice, piano, guitar and/or basic music classes NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.  This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.  Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate any and all job duties as necessary. Additional Information Base Pay From 15,000 Base Pay To 25,000"
    },
