    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=486900101": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Adjunct - Professor of Nursing, On Campus Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Adjunct - on campus Required Degree Masters Manage Others Yes Description EFFECTIVE DATE: August 1, 2026 FLSA STATUS: Exempt HOURS WORKED: TBD as course schedule and workload is determined This is an adjunct faculty position within the School of Health and Science, teaching undergraduate nursing courses on campus and/or supervising nursing students in clinical settings. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Department of Nursing Chair . SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Nursing, the Dean of the School of Health and Science, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: Student Workers or Teaching Assistants as applicable EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College. Regular attendance on campus or to a clinical site to complete job duties is required. Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and related software, printer, calculator, copy machines, Nursing Simulation Lab equipment and tools related to undergraduate teaching and research. Travel to clinical sites will also be required. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: · Teach courses within the prescribed nursing curriculum utilizing a variety of teaching methodologies to engage students in the learning process. · Facilitate student development of knowledge, skills, and demeanor required for professional practice as a nurse. · Supervise students in clinical settings if applicable to the teaching assignments. · Stay abreast of scholarly developments in specific and relevant fields as well as current teaching methodologies, curriculum development, and assessment. · Participate in measures to maintain compliance with Minnesota State Board of Nursing and Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education. · Support the mission, goals and objectives of Crown College. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: · Demonstrated experience and expertise in nursing with preference to experience teaching nursing courses at the college level · Prefer demonstrated experience in simulation labs · Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education · Established ability to work effectively as a team member · Demonstrate excellence and professionalism in spoken, written and electronic communication skills when with prospective and current students, faculty, and staff, as well as clinical agency representatives · Ability to or willingness to learn how to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith · Experience or willingness to learn how to evaluate students’ work and report results promptly · Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those required of an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time (in the classroom, in the simulation lab, and in clinical settings). Mobility to allow for safe movement within lab and clinical environments. Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for patient care, safe use of equipment, and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry. Vocal strength to speak clearly in a classroom and lab for extended periods of time . Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials. Body strength to frequently lift and/ or move up to ten (10) pounds. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: · Master of Science in Nursing or equivalent degree · Relevant experience as a nurse · Current unencumbered RN License · Current American Heart Association Healthcare Provider BLS Certification (or equivalent). PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): · Earned DNP, PhD in Nursing or other equivalent terminal degree · Experience as a nurse in acute medical/surgical, ICU, Emergency, or related area · Unencumbered RN Licensure in Minnesota · 3+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education · Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments, especially related to the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education and the Minnesota Board of Nursing NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.  This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.  Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate any and all job duties as necessary. Additional Information Base Pay From 800/Load hr Base Pay To 900/ Load hr"
    },
    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=486886168": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Faculty-in-Residence, Criminal Justice and Legal Studies Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Required Degree Masters Manage Others No Contact information Name Dr. Chris Mathews Email mathewsc@crown.edu Description EFFECTIVE DATE: July 1, 2026 FLSA STATUS: Exempt HOURS WORKED: 15-20 hours weekly during regular academic terms This is a part-time faculty position to teach undergraduate criminal justice courses on campus within the School of Liberal Arts and Education. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of the Department of Humanities and Social Science. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Humanities and Social Science , the Dean of the School of Liberal Arts and Education , and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: None. EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College.  Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and required programs, printer, fax machine, calculator, copy machines, and other equipment as the position requires. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: · Teach two courses per normal academic term related to criminal justice. Courses may include Criminal Procedure, Criminal Statues & Enforcement, and Criminal Investigations. · Hold an average of at least 6 office hours per week during the normal academic terms. Participate in department and faculty meetings as available Academic advising for Criminal Justice and Legal Studies students as needed REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES: · Demonstrated experience and expertise in teaching criminal justice courses at the college level · Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education · Established ability to work effectively as a team member · Demonstrate excellence in spoken, written and electronic communication skills · Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith · Experience evaluating students’ work and reporting results promptly · Hands-on experience in the criminal justice or legal field through previous work and/or consulting experience · Ability and willingness to stay abreast of the ever-changing criminal justice environment in order to maintain relevancy in teaching criminal justice courses to college-level students · Skill to organize and manage multiple tasks simultaneously · Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those required of an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time in classroom Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for safe use of equipment and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry Vocal strength to speak clearly in classroom for extended periods of time Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials Body strength to frequently lift and/or move up to twenty-five (25) pounds MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: · Master’s level degree in criminal justice or a related field, or Bachelor degree in relevant criminal justice-related field AND a minimum of 10 years’ direct experience in a relevant criminal justice-related field · Demonstrated teaching effectiveness · Work experience in criminal justice, law enforcement, law, corrections, or a related field · Experience using computer technology in the teaching/learning process PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): · A PhD or terminal degree in a related field · 5+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education · Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments · Experience with academic advising/mentoring NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. Additional Information Base Pay From 15,000 Base Pay To 25,000"
    },
    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=486886164": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position- Nursing Department Student Worker Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student Manage Others No Contact information Name Liz Rodgers Phone rodgerse@crown.edu Description Anticipated Start Date: September 2, 2026. The nursing department is seeking a detail-oriented student worker to assist in preparations for nursing laboratory and simulation experiences. This position supports the nursing professor in preparing for in-person laboratory and clinical simulation experiences. Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. Evidence of Christian character and a commitment to encourage others toward Christ-likeness. Maintain a 2.0 cumulative GPA. Must be in good standing with the college. Previous experience with administrative work preferred. Responsibilities - Provide a detailed list of tasks and responsibilities. Set up laboratory equipment in the nursing lab. Set up simulators, with the professor's help, for simulation experiences. Make copies of student materials for lab experiences. Support maintaining and cleaning the learning environment prior to and after the laboratory/simulation experience. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High attention to detail and accuracy in completing tasks. Proficiency with basic computer applications, including email and word processing. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Interpersonal skills. Strong customer service orientation with a friendly and helpful demeanor. Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities. Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team. Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace. Ability to follow safety and sanitation guidelines in all work areas. Physical ability to stand, walk, lift, and carry items up to 25 lbs. for extended periods. Physical Demands: Ability to move about campus and within work areas as required. Ability to lift and carry loads of up to 4 pounds. Ability to lift, carry, push, or pull items weighing up to 25 lbs. Ability to bend, stoop, reach, and perform repetitive motions as part of regular tasks. Ability to operate necessary equipment or tools safely in assigned work areas. Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay Per Hour"
    },
    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=453355349": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position- Student Receptionist Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student Contact information Name Brandon Schmidly Email schmidlyb@crown.edu Description Hours Worked Per Week up to 15-20 hours The Crown College Student Receptionist will provide professional and courteous service via the telephone and in person to the members of the College community and the public. They will portray an image of Crown College that is consistent with its mission and lifestyle standards. Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. Evidence of Christian character and a commitment to encourage others toward Christ-likeness. Must be in good standing with the college. Previous experience with administrative work preferred. Responsibilities - Provide a detailed list of tasks and responsibilities. • The student receptionist is immediately responsible to the Primary Receptionist • The student receptionist will promptly answer all calls and route them pleasantly and quickly • The student receptionist will assist visitors to the College, giving a pleasant greeting and offer of assistance. • The student receptionist will maintain familiarity with all current email and calendar information related to campus activity (guests, events, etc.) • The student receptionist will serve as the primary contact in the event of an emergency, assisting Student Development and Security personnel by conveying urgent information and contacting the appropriate emergency assistance • The student receptionist will process all incoming faxes electronically for college personnel and students • The student receptionist will issue temporary guest parking passes. • The student receptionist will maintain the professional appearance of the reception area by keeping it clean and free of unnecessary items • The student receptionist will maintain familiarity with the Receptionist Manual, attend all required meetings as scheduled, and fulfill all assigned shifts according to policy • The student receptionist will present a professional and appropriate personal appearance in keeping with scheduled campus events and according to the policy as listed in the Receptionist Manual • The student receptionist will perform various other tasks as requested by college personnel and as assigned by the Advancement Office. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High attention to detail and accuracy in completing tasks. Proficiency with basic computer applications, including email and word processing. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Interpersonal skills. Strong customer service orientation with a friendly and helpful demeanor. Maintain confidentiality regarding private student information. Demonstrated dependability and punctuality. Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities. Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team. Strong problem-solving skills and ability to respond appropriately to unexpected situations. Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace. Ability to follow safety and sanitation guidelines in all work areas. Physical Demands: Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while performing job duties. Preferred Qualifications: • Reliable, friendly, and professional • Extensive phone, office, and customer service experience Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay Per Hour"
    },
    "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=453337473": {
      "title": "CBIZ20706:Career Search",
      "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position- Content Creator (Campus Experience and Community Life) Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student Description The Student Content Creator will assist the Marketing Content Coordinator in providing content revolving around CAMPUS EXPERIENCE & COMMUNITY LIFE for social media channels in a variety of digital formats that accurately reflect Crown College. Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. Evidence of Christian character and a commitment to encourage others toward Christ-likeness. Maintain a 2.0 cumulative GPA. Must be in good standing with the college. Responsibilities - Provide a detailed list of tasks and responsibilities. Campus Experience Coverage - Capture authentic student-life moments: studying, hanging out, serving, worshiping, and celebrating together. - Highlight Student Life and Residence Life events that showcase community and connection. - Represent a wide range of students, majors, and activities. Faith Discovery - Document chapel, worship, service projects, and ministry events that reflect spiritual growth. - Capture stories that show faith lived out authentically across campus. Community & Collaboration - Partner with Student Life and Campus Ministries to plan coverage. - Collaborate weekly with the Academic & Athletics creator to align storytelling and maintain visual consistency. Content Contribution - Upload photos and video clips to the shared folder weekly. - Suggest captions or short-form post ideas that align with Crown’s “Life + Faith” storytelling wells. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High attention to detail and accuracy in completing tasks., Proficiency with basic computer applications, including email and word processing., Effective verbal and written communication skills. Interpersonal skills. Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities., Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team, Strong problem-solving skills and ability to respond appropriately to unexpected situations., Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace., Physical ability to stand, walk, lift, and carry items up to 25 lbs. for extended periods. Willingness to work a flexible schedule, including evenings or weekends as needed. Physical Demands: Ability to move about campus and within work areas as required., Ability to lift and carry loads of up to 4 pounds.? Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while performing job duties. Physically able to fulfill duties. Ability to bend, stoop, reach, and perform repetitive motions as part of regular tasks., Ability to operate necessary equipment or tools safely in assigned work areas. Preferred Qualifications: - Experience with Canva, Lightroom, or mobile editing apps (CapCut, Adobe Rush, VSCO) - Prior experience in photography, social media, or creative roles - Involvement in athletics, Student Life, or creative arts at Crown Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay Per Hour"
    },
